                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure M.—Translation from the Ferro Carril.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Words spoken by Don Domingo Arteagar, Alemparte, the
                        editor, at a large banquet given to the medical students who had acted nobly
                        during the epidemic.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1872-09-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#small-caps">September</hi> 4,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: I arise to propose a toast in honor
                    of the Honorable Mr. Root, minister of the United States. The Government of the
                    United States sent him to Chili to cultivate with our government the relations
                    of good-fellowship and harmony, which happily exist between the two
                    countries.</p>
                <p>In presence of the epidemic which afflicted us, Mr. Root contented not himself
                    alone with performing the duties of that noble mission. Disregarding the
                    advantages of his exalted position, the comforts and securities of his home, he
                    wished to cultivate also relations with the suffering and the contagion of our
                    city. He visited our lazarettos, he attended and aided our sick—compromised his
                    life by saving our lives. He has been thus something more than the diplomatic
                    representative of the great republic. He has been a man of charity.</p>
                <p>Gentlemen: To the health of Mr. Root, envoy extraordinary and minister
                    plenipotentiary of the human brotherhood, near the afflictions and sympathies of
                    the Chilian people.</p>
            </div>
